 ### SnowPakTool Desktop UI
 
-**Editors â†’ Frame addons** lists frame attachments, roof racks and service equipment using the same read-only table, description and source-property view as Addons and Cargo. The main table shows cargo slots, fuel/water capacity, repair points, spare wheels, price, unlock rank, exploration lock, install socket, content and ID, with shared column sorting/filtering. Selecting a row shows all XML properties and source files below. Explicit file parents supply inherited summary values; templates remain visible without expansion, so blank capacities are unresolved rather than assumed zero. Install sockets do not establish complete truck compatibility. Reload reads the current workspace in the background; no game data is edited.
+**Editors → Frame addons** lists frame attachments, roof racks and service equipment with the same table, description and source-property view as Addons and Cargo. The main table shows cargo slots, fuel/water capacity, repair points, spare wheels, price, unlock rank, exploration lock, install socket, content and ID, with shared column sorting/filtering. Selecting a row shows all XML properties and source files below. Explicit file parents supply inherited summary values; templates remain visible without expansion, so blanks are unresolved rather than assumed zero. Install sockets do not establish complete truck compatibility.
+
+The **Fuel multiplier** slider uses Truck properties' shared calculations: 0.5×–3× in 0.5 steps. Moving it only selects the factor; **Multiply all fuel** multiplies the current preview of every frame addon with a locally explicit fuel capacity and category, rounds to the nearest 5 litres (ties upward), and clamps to 5–100,000 L. Repeated clicks multiply again; column filters do not restrict the operation. Blank/inherited capacities stay unchanged. Changed fuel cells show the preserved original in parentheses, with amber preview/staged and green applied highlights. **Stage changes** saves an explicit snapshot across restarts; only **Start → Apply pending PAK edits** writes it to the updated overlay. Later previews do not change the staged snapshot. **Revert unstaged edits** restores that snapshot, **Revert staged changes** clears it, and **Reset to original values** previews rounded baseline capacities. Reload discards unstaged previews. Apply validates every fuel target before writing, preserves unrelated XML/templates and original files, and retains staged edits if a capacity changed externally.
 
 A **slot-based upgrade randomizer** is available in **Randomizer â†’ Upgrades**. Randomize upgrades builds the full component catalog from the workspace, resolves composite tire IDs, uses current obtainable map-truck previews plus direct garage/contract rewards, and saves a draft under `workspace/upgrade-randomization/draft.json`. Region progression must be finalized. Only owned regions are generated; replacement eligibility uses enabled trucks and explicit tire-pack ownership. Each pickup retains its original type, and metal detectors stay fixed. Truck-specific slots prefer unused local-compatible parts; shared slots use all eligible shared parts without a purchase-only restriction, with an extra foreign preference in the first region. Fallbacks broaden the same-type pool before reuse. Stock/default-only and objective-locked replacements are excluded conservatively. There is no locality quota. See [the planner and input contract](upgrade-distribution-draft.md).
 
